NAME
     crontab - a user's schedule

SYNOPSIS
     crontab [-u USER] [-l|-r|-e|FILE]

DESCRIPTION
     crontab installs, prints or removes the table of commands crond
     runs for a user. A line is five fields -- minute, hour, day of
     month, month, day of week -- and then the command.

OPTIONS
     -u USER   whose table (root only)
     -l        print it
     -r        remove it
     -e        edit it
     FILE      install this file as the table

SEE ALSO
     crond(8), sh(1)
